# Company-managed apps, installed by hand from Iru Self Service (Kandji).
# This file is that source. scripts/render-app-sources.sh reads the names into
# the README section "Where apps come from". Do not declare these in the
# Brewfile — mas can't upgrade root:wheel App Store copies
# ("No downloads initiated for ADAM ID …"), and brew bundle would then fail.
#
# Format: Name | /Applications/….app | optional-mas-id
# Blank lines and # comments ignored.
#
# A missing app is a warning: install from Iru Self Service.
# Do not add 1Password for Safari (id 1569813296) or Okta Extension App
# (id 1439967473). It isn't known whether Iru installs them, and a
# missing-app warning would be noise.
# Okta Verify is company-managed (App Store id 490179405). mas can't upgrade it.
Okta Verify|/Applications/Okta Verify.app|490179405
1Password|/Applications/1Password.app|
Tailscale|/Applications/Tailscale.app|
Zoom|/Applications/zoom.us.app|
Formal|/Applications/Formal.app|
Cyberhaven|/Applications/Cyberhaven.app|
